(2461057, 335672, 6388, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by aerogurl:</b></div><hr/><i> very nice! congrats on the ribbon. Did you get the idea from America''s Next Top Model? Their first photo shoot was to don bald head caps and pose with bald mannequins. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>not so much...reality TV and I don''t get along so well.  assumeing one might call that kind of show ''reality'' :P<br/> <br/>no, the idea came like most of them...out of the blue.  I had noticed that my friend had a bunch of those things at her house, and we already had the white face paint which was intended for another idea I had.  it literally went from idea to completion in about an hour and a half.<br/> <br/>thanks for the comments, y''all.<br/> <br/>P</td>', 'Originally posted by aerogurl: very nice! congrats on the ribbon. Did you get the idea from America''s Next Top Model? Their first photo shoot was to don bald head caps and pose with bald mannequins.   not so much...reality TV and I don''t get along so well.  assumeing one might call that kind of show ''reality'' :P no, the idea came like most of them...out of the blue.  I had noticed that my friend had a bunch of those things at her house, and we already had the white face paint which was intended for another idea I had.  it literally went from idea to completion in about an hour and a half. thanks for the comments, y''all. P', '2006-05-26 21:13:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2461061, 335951, 58861, '<td valign="top">I''ve seen a lot of pictures on this site with this kind of color, contrast and tones. Like  <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=334451" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this</a>, <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=334230" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this</a> and <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=333872" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this</a>. I''m very new to photoghaphy but this is the kind of effect I want to achieve. Is it done in post-processing or were they actually taken this way? If anyone could shed some light to help me out that would be great. Absolutely love this shot btw.</td>', 'I''ve seen a lot of pictures on this site with this kind of color, contrast and tones. Like  this, this and this. I''m very new to photoghaphy but this is the kind of effect I want to achieve. Is it done in post-processing or were they actually taken this way? If anyone could shed some light to help me out that would be great. Absolutely love this shot btw.', '2006-05-26 21:16:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2461074, 336288, 41337, '<td valign="top">I scored this image an 8 because it struck me as a great self portrait. I don''t know you well but for this moment in time the camera caught you I felt I did and that''s what makes a good self portrait, IMO. <br/> <br/>And for that effort what does DPC do in typical fashion? It places it 183rd. Good grief. Most of the images that ranked ahead of this could only dream of the substance this had but alas we as a community just want our daily fix of exploding landscape backdrops, cool looking props and super tack sharp eyeballs that were dodged and burned to mathematical perfection. It would be great if ONE TIME a challenge rewarded authenticity over the constant illusions that ribbon each week. <br/> <br/>Edited to add: Sorry about the rant. Just had to vent a bit. :) Oh and btw, there''s nothing technically with your photo in my opinion. To me it lives and breathes and tells a thousand words and that is all any photographer/photoshop artist could hope to acheive so well done!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-05-26 20:36:40.</i></td>', 'I scored this image an 8 because it struck me as a great self portrait. I don''t know you well but for this moment in time the camera caught you I felt I did and that''s what makes a good self portrait, IMO.  And for that effort what does DPC do in typical fashion? It places it 183rd. Good grief. Most of the images that ranked ahead of this could only dream of the substance this had but alas we as a community just want our daily fix of exploding landscape backdrops, cool looking props and super tack sharp eyeballs that were dodged and burned to mathematical perfection. It would be great if ONE TIME a challenge rewarded authenticity over the constant illusions that ribbon each week.  Edited to add: Sorry about the rant. Just had to vent a bit. :) Oh and btw, there''s nothing technically with your photo in my opinion. To me it lives and breathes and tells a thousand words and that is all any photographer/photoshop artist could hope to acheive so well done!', '2006-05-26 21:34:31.000000', '2006-05-26 21:36:40.000000', 0),
