(2461840, 335951, 1531, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by silenced:</b></div><hr/><i> I''ve seen a lot of pictures on this site with this kind of color, contrast and tones. Like  <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=334451" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this</a>, <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=334230" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this</a> and <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=333872" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this</a>. I''m very new to photoghaphy but this is the kind of effect I want to achieve. Is it done in post-processing or were they actually taken this way? If anyone could shed some light to help me out that would be great. Absolutely love this shot btw. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Not really sure, might be relatively more contrast than saturation or just the icelandic look ;-) (3/4 icelandic)</td>', 'Originally posted by silenced: I''ve seen a lot of pictures on this site with this kind of color, contrast and tones. Like  this, this and this. I''m very new to photoghaphy but this is the kind of effect I want to achieve. Is it done in post-processing or were they actually taken this way? If anyone could shed some light to help me out that would be great. Absolutely love this shot btw.   Not really sure, might be relatively more contrast than saturation or just the icelandic look ;-) (3/4 icelandic)', '2006-05-27 11:37:15.000000', NULL, 0),
