(2465960, 335951, 50432, '<td valign="top">From the photo of your set up, it looks as though you are at the edge of a very steep cliff.  Were you?  How did you make a jump like that from the ground?  Seems a jump like that would require something bouncy to jump from.  Did you have something?  Just curious.  It''s really an awesome shot.  Wish I was that good at it!</td>', 'From the photo of your set up, it looks as though you are at the edge of a very steep cliff.  Were you?  How did you make a jump like that from the ground?  Seems a jump like that would require something bouncy to jump from.  Did you have something?  Just curious.  It''s really an awesome shot.  Wish I was that good at it!', '2006-05-29 11:23:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2465989, 334765, 11518, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Artyste:</b></div><hr/><i> Well, you didn''t get that 8+ I predicted, but you came damn close.  Where the hell do you get all these props? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It''s not a "prop"...he sleeps with that axe under his pillow every night...:D</td>', 'Originally posted by Artyste: Well, you didn''t get that 8+ I predicted, but you came damn close.  Where the hell do you get all these props?   It''s not a "prop"...he sleeps with that axe under his pillow every night...:D', '2006-05-29 11:42:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(2466025, 335951, 58665, '<td valign="top">I have been meaning to send you a comment about this truly awesome shot.  Congratulations on a well thought out, technically challenging/excellent shot! You deserve the blue!  I am so envious of your beautiful icelandic landscapes.  Thanks for the set-up shot, helps dispel the backdrop theory.</td>', 'I have been meaning to send you a comment about this truly awesome shot.  Congratulations on a well thought out, technically challenging/excellent shot! You deserve the blue!  I am so envious of your beautiful icelandic landscapes.  Thanks for the set-up shot, helps dispel the backdrop theory.', '2006-05-29 12:09:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2466323, 335951, 1531, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by melissia:</b></div><hr/><i> From the photo of your set up, it looks as though you are at the edge of a very steep cliff.  Were you?  How did you make a jump like that from the ground?  Seems a jump like that would require something bouncy to jump from.  Did you have something?  Just curious.  It''s really an awesome shot.  Wish I was that good at it! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>True, I was one the edge. It wasn''t vertical, but still I''d rather not have fallen down. Actually I didn''t jump that high. As you can see on the setup photo the camera tripod is at it''s lowest position, and the wide angle lense (17mm) aimed upwards.</td>', 'Originally posted by melissia: From the photo of your set up, it looks as though you are at the edge of a very steep cliff.  Were you?  How did you make a jump like that from the ground?  Seems a jump like that would require something bouncy to jump from.  Did you have something?  Just curious.  It''s really an awesome shot.  Wish I was that good at it!   True, I was one the edge. It wasn''t vertical, but still I''d rather not have fallen down. Actually I didn''t jump that high. As you can see on the setup photo the camera tripod is at it''s lowest position, and the wide angle lense (17mm) aimed upwards.', '2006-05-29 14:08:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2466378, 333822, 31794, '<td valign="top">[[trading post]]<br/> <br/>this is a good portrait, but would have been better if you were on thr right side of the picture, to break the fundamentals of portraiture is very hard and the picture must have a big WOW factor to get away with breaking the rules, your image does unfortunately not have that WOW factor needed for this image to be great.<br/> <br/><a href="//rax.is/Gallery/ICELAND/ppages/ppage11.htm" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">image with WOW</a> <br/> <br/>here is a sample of a portrait where the subject looks outside the frame, and it works.<br/> <br/></td>', '[[trading post]] this is a good portrait, but would have been better if you were on thr right side of the picture, to break the fundamentals of portraiture is very hard and the picture must have a big WOW factor to get away with breaking the rules, your image does unfortunately not have that WOW factor needed for this image to be great. image with WOW  here is a sample of a portrait where the subject looks outside the frame, and it works. ', '2006-05-29 14:45:10.000000', NULL, 0),
